From da334d1297ca1895c46b14e1f00bb4893a2d173e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:38:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build(xtask): one cross-platform gate and decision collector

`cargo xtask gate quick|batch|release|test <name>` and `cargo xtask
decisions --version X.Y.Z` replace the gate.ps1/gate.sh and
collect-decisions.ps1/.sh twins with one Rust implementation in a new
workspace member `xtask/` (publish = false, alias in .cargo/config.toml).
It reproduces gate.ps1 (tiers, SLOW_BINARIES, crate lists, -j 6 / 6 test
threads, ui CWD, quick's diff-to-test-fn selection, logs, summary, exit
code); --dry-run output matches gate.ps1 -DryRun line for line for batch,
release, a sample quick diff and single tests. Two gate.ps1 -Test bugs
are fixed (a src/ tests module was planned as a nonexistent suite;
several lib files gave duplicate --lib steps). The old scripts are thin
wrappers that forward their flags. AGENTS.md, the gate-running agents and
skills name the one command; xtask/ and .cargo/config.toml join the fork
process-sync files; PROCESS_VERSION 7. release.ps1 stays as is (#749).

Refs #748

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
